1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:41,017
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:52,017
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:58,017
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,017 --> 00:03:09,017
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:13,017
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,017 --> 00:03:23,017
The first stop on Luffy's journey is Fishman Island, thousands of feet below sea level, where his crew becomes involved in a civil war.

8
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:26,017
Meeting Jinbei, they learn of the events that led to the conflict.

9
00:03:26,017 --> 00:03:33,017
He tells the tale of the Fishman Pirates, the island's brave queen, and its hero, Fisher Tiger.

10
00:03:37,017 --> 00:03:39,017
It's okay for you to cry!

11
00:03:40,017 --> 00:03:45,017
We are nothing like those evil celestial dragons, so don't you dare act like we are.

12
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,017
Now watch.

13
00:03:56,017 --> 00:04:03,017
No killing. Not now. Not ever. No matter how far the journey.

14
00:04:03,017 --> 00:04:07,017
We are taking this girl back home!

15
00:04:07,017 --> 00:04:13,017
The death of the hero! A shocking truth of Tiger!

16
00:04:13,017 --> 00:04:24,017
It took a while, but we finally got an eternal pose to Koala's hometown.

17
00:04:24,017 --> 00:04:28,017
Nyu! You hear that, Koala? You could go back to your family!

18
00:04:28,017 --> 00:04:30,017
Um, really?

19
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:34,017
Nyu! Ha-ha-ha!

20
00:04:35,017 --> 00:04:36,017
Well, aren't you pretty!

21
00:04:36,017 --> 00:04:39,017
Your parents will be proud to see what a fine young lady you become!

22
00:04:39,017 --> 00:04:43,017
I don't...look silly.

23
00:04:47,017 --> 00:04:50,017
We got rid of those old rags of yours. You don't want them back, right?

24
00:04:51,017 --> 00:04:52,017
Nyu!

25
00:04:52,017 --> 00:04:56,017
You may feel awkward at first, but I promise, your mom will be happy!

26
00:04:56,017 --> 00:05:01,017
I should clean!

27
00:05:02,017 --> 00:05:06,017
You! You gotta break that weird habit of yours, okay?

28
00:05:06,017 --> 00:05:09,017
You're just a normal girl. This isn't Marie Joie.

29
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:11,017
Ah, just let her do what she wants.

30
00:05:11,017 --> 00:05:12,017
You?

31
00:05:12,017 --> 00:05:15,017
The girl was traumatized. You can't expect her to stop that easily.

32
00:05:15,017 --> 00:05:17,017
These things take time.

33
00:05:17,017 --> 00:05:18,017
Sorry.

34
00:05:18,017 --> 00:05:21,017
You should listen to Aladdin. He would know.

35
00:05:21,017 --> 00:05:25,017
Yes. Because you were a slave once yourself, weren't you?

36
00:05:25,017 --> 00:05:29,017
But those feelings might be better served if you killed her.

37
00:05:30,017 --> 00:05:32,017
Former slave or not, she's human.

38
00:05:32,017 --> 00:05:34,017
Just like the ones who owned you.

39
00:05:34,017 --> 00:05:36,017
I think we've heard enough hour long.

40
00:05:36,017 --> 00:05:38,017
Let me ask you a little question.

41
00:05:38,017 --> 00:05:39,017
Tell me the truth.

42
00:05:39,017 --> 00:05:41,017
Even though we spared your life,

43
00:05:41,017 --> 00:05:44,017
I bet your parents don't give a damn about fishmen.

44
00:05:46,017 --> 00:05:52,017
Humans think they're superior to everyone.

45
00:05:52,017 --> 00:05:56,017
That's why there's no point in saving a so-called innocent child,

46
00:05:56,017 --> 00:05:57,017
because all of them are guilty.

47
00:05:57,017 --> 00:06:00,017
She'll go home and she'll learn to hate us.

48
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:03,017
It won't stop until we stop them.

49
00:06:03,017 --> 00:06:05,017
Until we take them down a peg.

50
00:06:06,017 --> 00:06:08,017
But you know that, right?

51
00:06:08,017 --> 00:06:11,017
You've seen the way they look at us, haven't you?

52
00:06:11,017 --> 00:06:15,017
The fear, the contempt in their eyes.

53
00:06:16,017 --> 00:06:20,017
If it were my decision, they would all be five feet under right now.

54
00:06:20,017 --> 00:06:35,017
Some humans, but hardly all of them.

55
00:06:35,017 --> 00:06:37,017
I think you need to look closer.

56
00:06:37,017 --> 00:06:38,017
Is that so?

57
00:06:38,017 --> 00:06:43,017
I see fear, but that is not the same as contempt.

58
00:06:48,017 --> 00:06:50,017
Is it because we're pirates?

59
00:06:53,017 --> 00:06:55,017
Why are you so afraid of us?

60
00:06:57,017 --> 00:06:58,017
Cause I...

61
00:06:59,017 --> 00:07:01,017
I don't know much about you.

62
00:07:01,017 --> 00:07:06,017
I've heard that before.

63
00:07:07,017 --> 00:07:10,017
It's true that our only exposure to humans has been negative,

64
00:07:10,017 --> 00:07:13,017
but that doesn't mean we can judge all humans the same.

65
00:07:16,017 --> 00:07:18,017
Fear comes from ignorance.

66
00:07:20,017 --> 00:07:22,017
Koala, let's play a game.

67
00:07:23,017 --> 00:07:26,017
See if you can figure out which hand it's in.

68
00:07:27,017 --> 00:07:29,017
There, okay, guess.

69
00:07:30,017 --> 00:07:31,017
Um...

70
00:07:32,017 --> 00:07:33,017
That one?

71
00:07:34,017 --> 00:07:35,017
Nope, too bad.

72
00:07:35,017 --> 00:07:36,017
Here it is.

73
00:07:39,017 --> 00:07:41,017
Okay, one more try.

74
00:07:42,017 --> 00:07:43,017
Alright, watch close.

75
00:07:46,017 --> 00:07:47,017
Now guess.

76
00:07:48,017 --> 00:07:49,017
Um... this one?

77
00:07:50,017 --> 00:07:51,017
Oh, so close.

78
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:57,017
Another place.

79
00:07:58,017 --> 00:08:02,017
Fuck out.

80
00:08:02,017 --> 00:08:03,017
The issue looks as though.

81
00:08:04,017 --> 00:08:09,017
Well and of his乱 répondre.

82
00:08:10,017 --> 00:08:11,017
Look it's pretty cool that a lot.

83
00:08:12,017 --> 00:08:14,017
What kind of encounter will it be?

84
00:08:15,017 --> 00:08:16,017
What's interesting?

85
00:08:17,017 --> 00:08:19,017
Am I striking out?

86
00:08:19,017 --> 00:08:20,017
The day as the night, the moon of a royal츠,

87
00:08:20,017 --> 00:08:21,017
the flame of a fallen was waiting for you.

88
00:08:21,017 --> 00:08:22,017
Girl of endeavors and Frolices.

89
00:08:23,017 --> 00:08:24,017
What kind of capture are lies without you?

90
00:08:24,017 --> 00:08:51,697
Then, just as she started to open up to the crew,

91
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:55,697
we reached her last stop, Full Shot Island.

92
00:08:55,697 --> 00:08:58,697
Her hometown at last, as promised.

93
00:08:58,697 --> 00:09:00,697
This is it, Koala.

94
00:09:00,697 --> 00:09:02,697
Time to bid the ship farewell.

95
00:09:08,697 --> 00:09:10,697
Where's your home village?

96
00:09:10,697 --> 00:09:13,697
Come on, I'll walk you to the entrance at least.

97
00:09:13,697 --> 00:09:14,697
Okay.

98
00:09:14,697 --> 00:09:18,697
Don't go, Koala. You can keep sailing with us.

99
00:09:18,697 --> 00:09:23,697
You're a good girl, even if you're human!

100
00:09:23,697 --> 00:09:25,697
Would you pull it together?

101
00:09:27,697 --> 00:09:30,697
I'll tell the whole village how great you guys are!

102
00:09:30,697 --> 00:09:34,697
I'll let everyone know that fishmen are nice and not scary!

103
00:09:37,697 --> 00:09:39,697
I'll miss you! So long!

104
00:09:39,697 --> 00:09:41,697
Thanks for helping me!

105
00:09:48,697 --> 00:09:50,697
Bye! Good luck out there!

106
00:09:51,697 --> 00:09:52,697
doing fun!

107
00:09:52,697 --> 00:09:53,697
Look out there!

108
00:09:53,697 --> 00:09:54,697
Yeah!

109
00:09:54,697 --> 00:09:56,697
.

110
00:10:08,697 --> 00:10:13,697
Hmm...

111
00:10:13,697 --> 00:10:27,557
You think she's cute now, but she'll be a fish man hating bigots soon enough.

112
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:29,857
Orlang, you take that back.

113
00:10:30,157 --> 00:10:30,397
Huh?

114
00:10:31,057 --> 00:10:31,657
Jinbei.

115
00:10:32,457 --> 00:10:33,977
Enough. All right?

116
00:10:34,197 --> 00:10:35,397
Always so noble.

117
00:10:36,897 --> 00:10:40,197
Funny. Three years ago, you weren't like this.

118
00:10:40,257 --> 00:10:40,897
What's that?

119
00:10:41,037 --> 00:10:42,057
Don't be a fool.

120
00:10:42,057 --> 00:10:47,037
One girl telling her village that fishmen are nice isn't going to change a thing.

121
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:50,097
Just like poor Queen Otahime.

122
00:10:50,497 --> 00:10:53,677
No one will listen, and no one will give a damn.

123
00:11:00,677 --> 00:11:01,737
It's Koala!

124
00:11:02,097 --> 00:11:05,237
She came back. Look, it's your daughter. Come and see for yourself.

125
00:11:07,337 --> 00:11:08,677
It is her.

126
00:11:09,057 --> 00:11:09,517
Yeah.

127
00:11:09,997 --> 00:11:10,877
Hey, guys!

128
00:11:10,877 --> 00:11:13,657
Hurry. Go and tell her low.

129
00:11:14,017 --> 00:11:14,577
Koala!

130
00:11:16,157 --> 00:11:17,317
You're home!

131
00:11:19,617 --> 00:11:20,177
Mom?

132
00:11:20,177 --> 00:11:36,277
I'm so glad you're back.

133
00:11:36,277 --> 00:11:39,637
I miss you so much!

134
00:11:39,637 --> 00:11:41,037
Mom! I love you!

135
00:11:41,037 --> 00:11:45,137
Mom! I love you!

136
00:11:47,677 --> 00:11:49,677
This is the best day!

137
00:11:50,317 --> 00:11:52,697
Hey, that's the captain of the Sun Pirates.

138
00:11:53,057 --> 00:11:54,177
Fish or tiger?

139
00:11:54,717 --> 00:11:56,837
Fish men are bad guys, aren't they?

140
00:11:57,097 --> 00:11:57,897
I'm scared.

141
00:11:57,897 --> 00:12:05,437
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you.

142
00:12:05,437 --> 00:12:09,277
I know you had an awful time, but you'll be safe with me now.

143
00:12:09,277 --> 00:12:10,977
Some good things happened, too.

144
00:12:11,817 --> 00:12:15,417
The nobles were mean, but I also made friends.

145
00:12:15,417 --> 00:12:20,617
Everyone said fish men are bad, but that's because they don't know them.

146
00:12:20,617 --> 00:12:23,157
I met a whole bunch of nice fish men.

147
00:12:23,157 --> 00:12:24,897
They're the ones who brought me here.

148
00:12:24,897 --> 00:12:27,497
I sailed for a long time with Uncle Tiger and all his friends.

149
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:28,497
If you got to know them, you'd like them, too.

150
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:29,497
That's all it takes.

151
00:12:29,497 --> 00:12:30,497
Uncle Tiger!

152
00:12:30,497 --> 00:12:32,497
You can't sneak off yet!

153
00:12:32,497 --> 00:12:33,497
Thanks! I'll miss you!

154
00:12:33,497 --> 00:12:34,497
Take care now!

155
00:12:34,497 --> 00:12:37,497
I'll never forget you, not for the rest of my life!

156
00:12:41,497 --> 00:12:43,497
And I won't forget Hachi or Aladdin either.

157
00:12:43,497 --> 00:12:44,497
Even if we never see each other again, we will be able to move on to the cloud.

158
00:12:44,497 --> 00:12:46,117
If you're not to know them, you'll be like them, too.

159
00:12:46,117 --> 00:12:47,077
Look.

160
00:12:47,077 --> 00:12:47,877
If you got to know them, you'd like them, too.

161
00:12:47,877 --> 00:12:48,837
That's all it takes.

162
00:12:48,837 --> 00:12:50,257
Uncle Tiger!

163
00:12:50,997 --> 00:12:52,377
You can't sneak off yet!

164
00:12:52,377 --> 00:12:53,377
Thanks! I'll miss you.

165
00:12:53,377 --> 00:12:54,257
Take care now!

166
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:58,877
I'll never forget you, not for the rest of my life!

167
00:12:59,077 --> 00:13:00,997
And I won't forget Hachi or Aladdin, either!

168
00:13:00,997 --> 00:13:03,957
Even if we never see each other again!

169
00:13:03,957 --> 00:13:21,957
I know these things happen slowly, but by the time you grow up, I hope our people can finally get along.

170
00:13:21,957 --> 00:13:37,957
Aha! There you are, Fisher Tiger of the Sun Pirates. I'm Rear Admiral Strawberry. We were informed that you might be stopping on this island.

171
00:13:37,957 --> 00:13:45,957
That girl was property of the Celestial Dragons, but we're going to look the other way on that matter, at least for the time being.

172
00:13:45,957 --> 00:13:52,957
That is to say, the village elders were more than willing to sell you out as long as we spared her.

173
00:13:52,957 --> 00:14:04,957
Do you know why I'm here? You must, so I won't waste your time. This is rather generous, all things considered, but you're facing two charges. Assault and escape.

174
00:14:15,957 --> 00:14:36,957
What the? What in the hell is going on?

175
00:14:36,957 --> 00:14:38,957
It's from the same direction Boss was headed.

176
00:14:38,957 --> 00:14:40,957
Surely they wouldn't attack him.

177
00:14:40,957 --> 00:14:43,957
Look! Out at sea!

178
00:14:43,957 --> 00:14:47,957
Two! It's the Navy! We're surrounded!

179
00:14:47,957 --> 00:14:49,957
What are they doing here?

180
00:14:49,957 --> 00:14:54,957
It was a damn trap! The brat was nothing but a ploy to lure us here!

181
00:14:54,957 --> 00:14:59,957
They played us for fools! We show them an ounce of kindness and this happens!

182
00:14:59,957 --> 00:15:03,957
See? Humans are monsters!

183
00:15:08,957 --> 00:15:17,957
Those bastards!

184
00:15:17,957 --> 00:15:21,957
Wait, no! It must be Tiger they want!

185
00:15:21,957 --> 00:15:26,957
Hey! You guys, guard the boat! I'm gonna go save the boss!

186
00:15:26,957 --> 00:15:33,957
Good! We finally agree! When you stop yapping and start throwing punches, I know you won't let me down!

187
00:15:33,957 --> 00:15:36,957
I'll take that as a compliment. Let's go!

188
00:15:36,957 --> 00:15:41,957
Hey, Arlong, sir! This is bad! The ship is gonna sink!

189
00:15:41,957 --> 00:15:44,957
Jump in the sea!

190
00:15:44,957 --> 00:15:49,957
Our ship's done for! Let's hijack one of theirs!

191
00:15:49,957 --> 00:16:04,957
How is this monster still fighting back? We're plugging him full of bullets and he's just shrugging it off!

192
00:16:07,957 --> 00:16:13,957
A monster? You humans think I'm a monster? We'll see!

193
00:16:13,957 --> 00:16:15,957
Fire!

194
00:16:21,957 --> 00:16:24,957
Did you hear that noise, Mom? It was loud!

195
00:16:25,957 --> 00:16:26,957
What noise?

196
00:16:28,957 --> 00:16:31,957
I was right! Boss!

197
00:16:32,957 --> 00:16:35,957
Rear Admiral, sir! The Sun Pirates came to save Tiger!

198
00:16:35,957 --> 00:16:40,957
I see. It's him. Yes. Team Bay!

199
00:16:45,957 --> 00:16:48,957
My friends, I'm sorry.

200
00:16:51,957 --> 00:16:53,957
Are you the one responsible for this?

201
00:16:53,957 --> 00:16:58,957
I do it all for justice. And justice demands I crush criminals like you!

202
00:16:58,957 --> 00:16:59,957
Curse you!

203
00:17:02,957 --> 00:17:04,957
Do you want to die with your captain?

204
00:17:04,957 --> 00:17:06,957
You're not as strong as you think, human!

205
00:17:06,957 --> 00:17:19,957
We were able to rescue our boss from the Marines as planned. And although our ship was sucked during battle, Arlong was able to secure a new one from the enemy.

206
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:22,957
Then...

207
00:17:22,957 --> 00:17:27,957
What?!

208
00:17:28,957 --> 00:17:33,957
What do you mean you don't want a transfusion? Are you crazy? You don't have time! You're gonna die!

209
00:17:33,957 --> 00:17:37,957
You've lost far too much blood! Whatever your feelings are, you must reconsider!

210
00:17:38,957 --> 00:17:43,957
The boss has a very rare blood type. No one on the crew is compatible, so we need another option!

211
00:17:43,957 --> 00:17:52,957
The blood they have stocked on the ship wouldn't be from fishmen. It would be... human.

212
00:17:53,957 --> 00:18:01,957
So what? It should work. Humans and fishmen share the same blood. We found your type as well. So it's settled, alright?

213
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:05,957
Now just relax. You're all good.

214
00:18:06,957 --> 00:18:07,957
Get away!

215
00:18:08,957 --> 00:18:11,957
I would rather die than live with their blood.

216
00:18:11,957 --> 00:18:21,957
I won't put that filth in my body. The blood of the bastards who tried to kill me.

217
00:18:22,957 --> 00:18:23,957
Dammit, no!

218
00:18:24,957 --> 00:18:31,957
I won't take their mercy. I will not owe them. I won't give in to any human! I won't!

219
00:18:34,957 --> 00:18:38,957
What happened? Something changed for you to say this!

220
00:18:41,957 --> 00:18:51,957
I didn't want... to tell you guys this... but I... on my last trip...

221
00:18:52,957 --> 00:18:54,957
That was quite a lengthy voyage you took!

222
00:18:55,957 --> 00:18:57,957
Yeah, an eventful one too.

223
00:18:58,957 --> 00:19:03,957
Tell me, why are you so adamant about this? What did you see on your trip?

224
00:19:03,957 --> 00:19:04,957
I saw human nature.

225
00:19:04,957 --> 00:19:28,957
Soon after I started off on my journey... they captured me... in Mariejoie. They made me... I was... a damn slave!

226
00:19:28,957 --> 00:19:29,957
Boss, no!

227
00:19:29,957 --> 00:19:30,957
Boss, no!

228
00:19:34,957 --> 00:19:49,957
Tiger! I saw true human corruption. True depravity. I barely escaped. But then... I kept thinking about those other slaves. So I went back.

229
00:19:49,957 --> 00:20:09,957
Listen to me. I lived... how I chose to. Against... Otohime's will. But... I still believe in her. I still believe that she's right.

230
00:20:09,957 --> 00:20:27,957
Everyone wants peace. Humans and fishmen alike. But our generation can't bring that peace. We're bound to an ugly past. Only children like Koala, free of that history, can change the world.

231
00:20:27,957 --> 00:20:42,957
Please. You can't... tell them. You... have to... hold it in. Our tragedy... and our hatred... they must die with us.

232
00:20:42,957 --> 00:20:44,957
No, it's all wrong!

233
00:20:44,957 --> 00:20:45,957
You heard me!

234
00:20:45,957 --> 00:21:06,957
Some humans... are kind. They know. We're not so different. I know it too. And because I've met so many compassionate humans, I realize it's foolish to leave nothing but hatred as legacy when I die.

235
00:21:06,957 --> 00:21:21,957
But even though my mind understands that, there is a devil in my heart that cannot forgive. That fills me with rage. My very flesh rejects them. It rejects their blood.

236
00:21:23,957 --> 00:21:29,957
Despite all that I've fought for, I cannot love them. I'm sorry!

237
00:21:29,957 --> 00:21:30,957
I'm sorry!

238
00:21:32,957 --> 00:21:38,957
However you feel, you can work it out when this is all done. For now, I'm begging you, just live!

239
00:21:39,957 --> 00:21:51,957
Listen, boss. You're a hero. Those slaves that you set free, they owe you their very lives. Please, boss, you can't die. Not like this. To every slave and every fishman, you're a symbol of hope.

240
00:21:52,957 --> 00:21:54,957
Then I'm happy.

241
00:21:54,957 --> 00:21:57,957
You're still not strong enough.

242
00:21:57,957 --> 00:21:58,957
Damn it!

243
00:21:58,957 --> 00:22:03,957
You have to step in front of your men, with your whole body. Do that. You protect them.

244
00:22:04,957 --> 00:22:05,957
Huh? Why would I...

245
00:22:07,957 --> 00:22:08,957
